1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,270
Two experts. Two opposite calls. Eight weeks.

2
00:00:03,540 --> 00:00:07,080
Robert Pape, one of America's top experts on war and bombing,

3
00:00:06,930 --> 00:00:10,610
says we've just entered the eight most dangerous weeks since this war

4
00:00:10,460 --> 00:00:11,100
began.

5
00:00:11,320 --> 00:00:15,370
Professor Jiang, the man who called Trump's comeback and the Iran war,

6
00:00:15,390 --> 00:00:19,290
says the exact opposite. These next two months will be fairly quiet.

7
00:00:19,620 --> 00:00:23,340
They can't both be right. And the answer moves oil, gold,

8
00:00:23,190 --> 00:00:24,000
and your money.

9
00:00:24,170 --> 00:00:27,870
Today we put both calls side by side, check them against history,

10
00:00:27,720 --> 00:00:31,310
and set the tests. On January third, we score them.

11
00:00:31,590 --> 00:00:35,110
This is The Arab Ledger. I'm Tall. Let's go.

12
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:38,110
First, who are these two men?

13
00:00:38,600 --> 00:00:42,340
Robert Pape teaches political science at the University of Chicago.

14
00:00:42,510 --> 00:00:46,720
He wrote Bombing to Win, a book on why bombing campaigns so

15
00:00:46,570 --> 00:00:47,420
often fail.

16
00:00:47,580 --> 00:00:49,710
He's been warning about this war all year.

17
00:00:50,060 --> 00:00:53,510
In July he put the risk of US ground operations in Iran

18
00:00:53,360 --> 00:00:54,970
at about seventy percent.

19
00:00:55,240 --> 00:00:58,480
So far, no US ground invasion has been reported.

20
00:00:58,650 --> 00:01:02,320
Professor Jiang runs the YouTube channel Predictive History,

21
00:01:02,370 --> 00:01:04,370
with nearly three million subscribers.

22
00:01:04,650 --> 00:01:08,270
He called Trump's comeback. He called a US war with Iran.

23
00:01:08,480 --> 00:01:10,630
And this week, he did something rare.

24
00:01:10,790 --> 00:01:13,070
He opened his new video with three words.

25
00:01:13,240 --> 00:01:14,220
I was wrong.

26
00:01:14,450 --> 00:01:17,660
Wrong about the midterms. Wrong about Brazil's election.

27
00:01:17,960 --> 00:01:20,330
Wrong about Alberta's independence vote.

28
00:01:20,550 --> 00:01:23,170
An independent fan site tracks his calls.

29
00:01:23,440 --> 00:01:27,560
Of the twenty-two that have been settled, it scores seventeen right.

30
00:01:27,760 --> 00:01:28,760
That's a small sample.

31
00:01:29,100 --> 00:01:30,870
So both men have hits and misses.

32
00:01:31,360 --> 00:01:34,580
Which is exactly why we test the claim, not the name.

33
00:01:35,500 --> 00:01:37,100
Here's Pape's call, in his words.

34
00:01:37,320 --> 00:01:40,460
We are about to enter the eight most dangerous weeks since this

35
00:01:40,310 --> 00:01:41,230
war began.

36
00:01:41,450 --> 00:01:43,980
The window: from the midterms on November third,

37
00:01:43,830 --> 00:01:47,270
until the new Congress is sworn in, around January third.

38
00:01:47,560 --> 00:01:52,050
His reasoning: President Trump has promised over and over and over again

39
00:01:52,140 --> 00:01:54,380
that he will escalate after the elections.

40
00:01:54,700 --> 00:01:57,680
He expects a short bombing plan that turns into a long one.

41
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:01,990
He points to nineteen ninety-one. The air campaign against Iraq, he says,

42
00:02:01,990 --> 00:02:05,680
was planned as three days. It went on for forty-three days.

43
00:02:05,940 --> 00:02:10,520
Let's check that. The Gulf War began on January seventeenth, nineteen ninety-one,

44
00:02:10,620 --> 00:02:15,660
and the ceasefire came on February twenty-eighth. Forty-three days. Correct.

45
00:02:15,980 --> 00:02:19,160
But one detail matters. The last four of those days were a

46
00:02:19,010 --> 00:02:22,670
planned ground war. So the war wasn't only bombing that dragged on.

47
00:02:22,760 --> 00:02:24,670
It was bombing, then troops.

48
00:02:24,870 --> 00:02:30,540
Which is exactly Pape's point about Iran. Bombing first. Then ground forces.

49
00:02:30,860 --> 00:02:34,780
He expects ground forces next. I think this is why the Marines

50
00:02:34,630 --> 00:02:35,350
are moving.

51
00:02:35,600 --> 00:02:37,710
And he sees Russia using the same window.

52
00:02:38,170 --> 00:02:42,360
Right around Thanksgiving, he expects strikes aimed at knocking out ninety percent

53
00:02:42,210 --> 00:02:44,360
of the power in Ukraine's big cities.

54
00:02:44,570 --> 00:02:47,280
For your money, he expects diesel prices to go up,

55
00:02:47,130 --> 00:02:50,140
and a frozen US housing market to freeze up even more.

56
00:02:50,530 --> 00:02:54,620
And if nothing changes, he warns of a devastating twenty twenty-seven.

57
00:02:55,500 --> 00:02:58,720
Now Jiang. Same eight weeks. Opposite call.

58
00:02:58,940 --> 00:03:03,190
His reasoning is about Congress. Only Congress can declare war,

59
00:03:03,300 --> 00:03:05,180
and it has never authorized this one.

60
00:03:05,530 --> 00:03:08,090
Jiang thinks the new Congress will authorize it,

61
00:03:08,230 --> 00:03:11,070
and that Trump will wait for that before any big move.

62
00:03:11,300 --> 00:03:14,260
For these next two months, before Congress is sworn in,

63
00:03:14,380 --> 00:03:16,950
there will be no major escalation of this war.

64
00:03:17,290 --> 00:03:21,080
He even defines what he means by escalation. Three things.

65
00:03:21,400 --> 00:03:26,300
One: a strike on Pickaxe Mountain, Iran's underground nuclear site near Natanz.

66
00:03:27,020 --> 00:03:30,710
It's buried deep under a mountain. In July,

67
00:03:30,560 --> 00:03:32,600
Trump publicly threatened to hit it.

68
00:03:32,840 --> 00:03:36,960
Two: Marines seizing Kharg Island or Qeshm Island.

69
00:03:37,140 --> 00:03:40,670
Kharg is Iran's oil export terminal. In March,

70
00:03:40,720 --> 00:03:44,870
the US bombed military targets there, but left the oil terminal standing.

71
00:03:45,300 --> 00:03:49,000
Qeshm is Iran's biggest island, sitting right at the mouth of the

72
00:03:48,850 --> 00:03:50,270
Strait of Hormuz.

73
00:03:50,500 --> 00:03:55,620
Three: a major bombing campaign against Iran's power plants and desalination plants.

74
00:03:55,950 --> 00:03:57,670
None of this will happen, he says.

75
00:03:57,850 --> 00:04:00,220
These next two months will be fairly quiet.

76
00:04:00,450 --> 00:04:03,990
But he's not calling for peace. He says after January,

77
00:04:04,190 --> 00:04:08,290
all bets are off. And by March, US ground troops in Iran.

78
00:04:08,520 --> 00:04:10,540
So the two men agree on where this goes.

79
00:04:10,830 --> 00:04:12,530
They disagree on when.

80
00:04:13,470 --> 00:04:15,260
So where are we, three days in?

81
00:04:15,720 --> 00:04:17,930
On November third, the day of the vote,

82
00:04:18,040 --> 00:04:22,260
the US struck Iran's Qeshm Island. A limited strike.

83
00:04:22,500 --> 00:04:26,040
The same day, Trump told the Financial Times he had no immediate

84
00:04:25,890 --> 00:04:28,310
plans for new strikes. But, quote,

85
00:04:28,380 --> 00:04:30,540
we're locked and loaded if we need to go.

86
00:04:30,820 --> 00:04:34,020
His vice president, J. D. Vance, is pushing for a deal.

87
00:04:34,300 --> 00:04:36,510
Qatar is mediating a draft agreement.

88
00:04:36,800 --> 00:04:40,680
Meanwhile, tankers have been hit near the Strait of Hormuz and off

89
00:04:40,530 --> 00:04:44,750
Qatar. Ship traffic through the strait is under sixty percent of normal.

90
00:04:45,040 --> 00:04:49,730
So far, it looks more like Jiang's flare-ups than Pape's big escalation.

91
00:04:50,170 --> 00:04:52,560
But it's day three of fifty-six.

92
00:04:52,780 --> 00:04:55,180
And remember the scoring is strict.

93
00:04:55,470 --> 00:04:58,730
A strike on Qeshm by itself isn't one of Jiang's three red

94
00:04:58,580 --> 00:05:00,550
lines. Seizing it would be.

95
00:05:01,450 --> 00:05:05,910
Now let's check both calls against history. Is this window really quiet?

96
00:05:06,400 --> 00:05:10,280
The period between a midterm election and the new Congress has a

97
00:05:10,130 --> 00:05:13,080
name in Washington. The lame duck.

98
00:05:13,330 --> 00:05:16,690
December nineteen ninety-eight. A lame-duck period.

99
00:05:16,890 --> 00:05:20,060
And the US and Britain bombed Iraq for four days.

100
00:05:20,290 --> 00:05:21,870
Operation Desert Fox.

101
00:05:22,210 --> 00:05:25,660
It started the same week the House voted to impeach President Clinton.

102
00:05:25,950 --> 00:05:30,650
January nineteen ninety-three. An outgoing President Bush ordered strikes on Iraq,

103
00:05:30,630 --> 00:05:32,190
days before he left office.

104
00:05:32,450 --> 00:05:36,830
So history says this window is not automatically quiet.

105
00:05:37,130 --> 00:05:38,920
Presidents have used it to strike.

106
00:05:39,260 --> 00:05:44,780
Point for Pape. But both of those were short, limited campaigns. Days,

107
00:05:44,630 --> 00:05:45,430
not weeks.

108
00:05:45,630 --> 00:05:49,580
That's closer to Jiang's there may be some bombings than to Pape's

109
00:05:49,430 --> 00:05:50,530
forty-three days.

110
00:05:51,460 --> 00:05:54,570
Now, the money. What do markets think?

111
00:05:55,000 --> 00:05:58,250
The day after the vote, oil fell eight percent.

112
00:05:58,680 --> 00:06:01,470
Brent dropped below a hundred dollars for the first time since early

113
00:06:01,320 --> 00:06:01,970
October.

114
00:06:02,290 --> 00:06:05,720
By Thursday it touched ninety-three. Down from a peak near one hundred

115
00:06:05,570 --> 00:06:06,390
and eighteen.

116
00:06:06,590 --> 00:06:10,980
That's the market betting on Jiang. Less war, more oil flowing.

117
00:06:11,200 --> 00:06:13,420
But by Friday, after more ships were hit,

118
00:06:13,520 --> 00:06:15,280
Brent was back near a hundred.

119
00:06:15,460 --> 00:06:16,840
So the market isn't sure either.

120
00:06:17,160 --> 00:06:19,090
And here's why the stakes are so high.

121
00:06:19,350 --> 00:06:22,500
Before this war, about a fifth of all the oil the world

122
00:06:22,350 --> 00:06:25,470
uses passed through the Strait of Hormuz every day.

123
00:06:25,770 --> 00:06:29,590
Today, ship traffic there is running at under sixty percent of normal.

124
00:06:29,860 --> 00:06:32,680
Every tanker that's hit pushes insurance costs up again.

125
00:06:32,960 --> 00:06:36,610
Kharg Island is the terminal that handles nearly all of Iran's oil

126
00:06:36,460 --> 00:06:37,190
exports.

127
00:06:37,530 --> 00:06:41,000
If Marines seize it, as Jiang says won't happen and Pape's logic

128
00:06:40,850 --> 00:06:44,080
suggests could, that oil goes offline overnight.

129
00:06:44,290 --> 00:06:46,220
If the power and water plants are hit,

130
00:06:46,490 --> 00:06:48,500
the war widens across the Gulf.

131
00:06:48,800 --> 00:06:53,990
In Pape's world: oil spikes, gold rises, stocks fall. In Jiang's world:

132
00:06:53,840 --> 00:06:57,650
oil drifts lower until January. Then the risk comes back.

133
00:06:58,540 --> 00:07:00,980
Here's how it looks from our side of the world.

134
00:07:01,260 --> 00:07:05,090
Every scenario in this video runs through our region. The strait,

135
00:07:04,940 --> 00:07:07,430
the tankers, the islands, the mediators in Doha.

136
00:07:07,720 --> 00:07:12,110
This week, Saudi Arabia intercepted missiles and drones fired by the Houthis.

137
00:07:12,720 --> 00:07:17,120
For Gulf economies, a quiet eight weeks means oil money keeps flowing

138
00:07:17,080 --> 00:07:18,750
and shipping slowly comes back.

139
00:07:19,080 --> 00:07:23,240
A loud eight weeks means the region pays first. In shipping,

140
00:07:23,300 --> 00:07:26,490
in insurance, in the price of everything that comes through the strait.

141
00:07:26,830 --> 00:07:30,090
And for importers like Morocco, every ten dollars on a barrel of

142
00:07:29,940 --> 00:07:32,690
oil shows up at the pump, and in the budget.

143
00:07:33,600 --> 00:07:35,340
From the person behind this channel.

144
00:07:35,580 --> 00:07:38,270
Don't watch the headlines. Watch the markets.

145
00:07:38,640 --> 00:07:41,490
If oil jumps and stock indexes fall hard,

146
00:07:41,680 --> 00:07:43,070
the market is pricing in Pape.

147
00:07:43,450 --> 00:07:46,410
If oil keeps sliding and indexes keep climbing,

148
00:07:46,660 --> 00:07:48,560
Jiang is closer to right.

149
00:07:48,830 --> 00:07:52,230
And if the political temperature in Washington starts rising after the vote,

150
00:07:52,400 --> 00:07:53,800
that tips it toward Pape.

151
00:07:54,340 --> 00:07:57,210
But honestly? The world will keep turning either way.

152
00:07:57,560 --> 00:08:01,990
So use this moment to build yourself. Your skills, your wealth,

153
00:08:02,120 --> 00:08:03,320
something that lasts.

154
00:08:03,640 --> 00:08:05,850
Whatever happens, come out of it stronger.

155
00:08:06,780 --> 00:08:10,890
So here are the tests. Five things to watch before January third.

156
00:08:11,890 --> 00:08:15,740
One: a major US bombing campaign against Iran's power or water plants.

157
00:08:15,840 --> 00:08:18,260
Pape says likely. Jiang says no.

158
00:08:19,260 --> 00:08:23,460
Two: US forces seizing Kharg or Qeshm Island. Pape points that way.

159
00:08:23,710 --> 00:08:25,720
Jiang says no.

160
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:29,730
Three: a strike on Pickaxe Mountain. Jiang says no.

161
00:08:29,900 --> 00:08:33,300
Four: Russian strikes that knock out most of the power in Ukraine's

162
00:08:33,150 --> 00:08:36,430
big cities around Thanksgiving. Pape says yes.

163
00:08:36,710 --> 00:08:41,020
Five: Brent above a hundred and ten dollars. Pape's world says yes.

164
00:08:41,170 --> 00:08:42,590
Jiang's world says no.

165
00:08:42,790 --> 00:08:46,500
If most of these happen, Pape wins. If none of them happen,

166
00:08:46,650 --> 00:08:47,890
Jiang wins.

167
00:08:48,080 --> 00:08:50,900
Either way, we'll be back on January third with the score.

168
00:08:51,180 --> 00:08:55,260
And we won't stop there. Jiang says US ground troops in Iran

169
00:08:55,110 --> 00:08:58,740
by March. Pape says twenty twenty-seven gets worse.

170
00:08:59,060 --> 00:09:00,970
Those calls go on our list too.

171
00:09:01,440 --> 00:09:04,310
We'll track every one of them, right or wrong, on this channel.

172
00:09:05,200 --> 00:09:08,550
So what does a careful person do with eight weeks like this?

173
00:09:08,970 --> 00:09:12,330
One: if you need fuel or travel in the next two months,

174
00:09:12,530 --> 00:09:15,750
remember that oil just swung twenty-five dollars in a few weeks.

175
00:09:16,160 --> 00:09:18,080
Don't assume today's price lasts.

176
00:09:18,320 --> 00:09:21,280
Two: don't bet everything on one forecaster.

177
00:09:21,680 --> 00:09:23,700
Pape and Jiang are both smart,

178
00:09:23,830 --> 00:09:25,160
and both have been wrong this year.

179
00:09:25,540 --> 00:09:30,640
Three: watch three numbers. The price of Brent. Ship traffic through Hormuz.

180
00:09:30,740 --> 00:09:33,160
And news from the talks in Doha.

181
00:09:33,510 --> 00:09:36,020
If all three move the wrong way together,

182
00:09:35,870 --> 00:09:40,610
Pape's eight weeks have started. If they stay calm, Jiang is winning.

183
00:09:41,540 --> 00:09:44,210
So who do you believe? Pape or Jiang?

184
00:09:44,460 --> 00:09:45,980
Write the name in the comments.

185
00:09:46,150 --> 00:09:48,560
If this helped you see the next eight weeks more clearly,

186
00:09:48,590 --> 00:09:51,710
like the video. It tells YouTube to show it to more people.

187
00:09:51,980 --> 00:09:54,620
And subscribe, so you see the score in January.

188
00:09:54,890 --> 00:09:58,200
This is education, not financial advice.

189
00:09:58,550 --> 00:10:00,410
Same world. Different lens.
